    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2S93TVbsGC5xPCxnTXaq4qi)_\n\n## What\n- Moved these reports onto `sp-batch-report-mode`. Their keys (`d` drop, `u` restore, `A` apply, `g`, `RET`, `n`/`p`) are now the shared ones:\n  - author notes report (kept its key filtering and text properties)\n  - footnote lint (`a` applies the plan)\n  - tag lint (`a` registers a tag)\n  - Org normalise report\n- The old views stay and are marked obsolete (`make-obsolete`): `sp-author-notes-report-mode`, `sp-org-lint-fn-report-mode`, `sp-org-tag-lint-report-mode`, `sp-org-normalise-report-mode`. New option `sp-batch-report-interface` (`new` by default, `old` brings them back) so both can be compared on the same run.\n- The #351 reports gained drop/restore/apply: litnote titles, litnote references, litnote meta fill-all, notes filing and the property conversion preview. A dropped file leaves the list, and `A` converts only the rest.\n- `sp-batch-report-key-entries` and `sp-batch-report-without-excluded` let reports built as plain text get keys without changing their text.\n- The BibTeX lint already moved in #352 (no old view left), so it is not touched here.\n- Not ported: the litnote status table (a table to edit, not a report), the keyword conversion preview (read before a `y-or-n-p`, so no key can be pressed), `sp-author-notes-works-dryrun` (a one-line message).\n\n## Tests\n- New tests for the shared keys in each ported report, and drop/apply tests for titles, refs, meta, notes filing and the property preview. All suites for touched modules pass in Emacs 29, except two failures that are not from this change: `sp-litnotes-titles-bib-authors-surname` (fails on `main` too) and `sp-org-lint-footnote-async-scan-and-apply` (the worker Emacs has no `sp-var-dir` here).\n- Docs tangle to the `.el` files (whitespace aside).\n- Not run on the real vault or in Emacs 31.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits, per the nightly-tidy rule.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAL5ZmmWoUzkvAu37X)_",
